    <h2 class="text-[28px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-[36px]">
      A free JSON diff checker built for speed and privacy
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-body">
      <p>
        JSON Diff Checker is a free <strong class="text-ink">JSON diff checker online</strong> that lets you
        compare two JSON files or objects and instantly see what changed. Paste your data, upload files, or
        load JSON straight from a URL, and this <strong class="text-ink">json diff tool</strong> highlights every
        added key, removed key, and changed value in a clean, color-coded tree — no installation, no account,
        and no data ever leaving your browser.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most teams need to <strong class="text-ink">compare json online</strong> at some point — checking an API
        response against a fixture, reviewing a config change before a deploy, or tracking down why two payloads
        that "should" be identical actually aren't. Doing this by eye in a text editor is slow and error-prone,
        especially with deeply nested objects or large arrays. This <strong class="text-ink">json comparison tool</strong>
        does the matching for you: keys are compared semantically rather than as raw text, so reordering keys
        inside an object never produces a false difference. If you need to <strong class="text-ink">compare two json
        files</strong> that only differ in formatting or key order, the diff stays focused on changes that
        actually matter.
      </p>

      <p>
        Arrays get the same careful treatment. By default, order matters — comparing
        <code class="rounded-sm bg-hairline-soft px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[13px]">["a","b"]</code> against
        <code class="rounded-sm bg-hairline-soft px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[13px]">["b","a"]</code> is reported as
        a change, since sequence often carries real meaning. But when you just need to
        <strong class="text-ink">compare json objects online</strong> without caring about array order, flip on
        "Ignore array order" and the tool matches array elements by an id/key field when one exists, or by value
        otherwise — so shuffled lists no longer show as noisy false positives. That makes this
        <strong class="text-ink">json diff viewer</strong> reliable for real-world API responses, where array
        ordering is frequently inconsistent between requests.
      </p>

      <p>
        As a <strong class="text-ink">free json diff checker</strong>, there's no paywall, no usage limit, and no
        watermark on exported results. Unlike many "free" tools online that quietly send your data to a server for
        processing, everything here runs client-side with plain JavaScript — open your browser's developer tools
        and watch the Network tab while you compare data, and you'll see nothing leave the page. That makes it
        safe to use as a <strong class="text-ink">json diff checker online free</strong> even with sensitive
        payloads: API tokens in test fixtures, internal config, or customer data you'd never want touching a
        third-party server.
      </p>

      <p>
        Beyond a basic <strong class="text-ink">json compare tool</strong>, this app is built to handle real
        production use cases. Invalid input doesn't just fail silently — you get the exact line and column where
        parsing broke, so fixing a missing comma or an unquoted key takes seconds instead of a manual scan through
        minified text. When you need to <strong class="text-ink">compare json files online</strong> that are large
        or deeply nested, the diff renders as a collapsible tree so the page stays readable and responsive instead
        of turning into a mile-long wall of text. Keyboard shortcuts let you jump between differences with Enter
        and Shift+Enter, and clicking any row copies its JSON Pointer path for pasting straight into a bug report
        or pull request.
      </p>

      <p>
        This is also a practical <strong class="text-ink">json diff generator</strong> for documentation and code
